sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-wavelength> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis>;
    dc:description "The spacing of a Turing pattern at onset is set by the reaction rates and diffusivities, not by the size of the tissue, so changing these parameters predictably changes the number of repeated elements.";
    dc:source "Alan Turing (1952) The chemical basis of morphogenesis";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Turing wavelength selection";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>, <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "at onset k_c^2 = \\sqrt{\\det J/(D_u D_v)}, \\lambda_c = 2\\pi/k_c; under uniform rescaling of D, \\lambda \\propto \\sqrt{D}";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: near onset of instability, two species, domain large compared with the wavelength. Formal status: proved by linear analysis. Away from onset, the selected wavelength depends on nonlinear terms and history.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Alter morphogen production, degradation or diffusion in a developing tissue (e.g. Hox dosage or Bmp/Wnt inhibition in mouse limb buds) and test whether digit or element number changes in the direction and proportion the dispersion relation predicts."
}
